menu "X/YModem"
    config XYMODEM_CANCEL_CAN_COUNT
        int "Number of <CAN> characters sent when canceling transmission"
        range 2 8
        default 2
        help
            X/YMODEM commonly uses two consecutive <CAN> characters to indicate
            transmission cancellation. Requiring multiple <CAN> characters reduces
            the risk of accidental cancellation caused by line errors.

            Sending additional <CAN> characters can make cancellation more reliable
            on noisy links, and some X/YMODEM specifications recommend sending eight
            <CAN> characters when aborting a transmission. This option specifies how
            many consecutive <CAN> characters are sent when canceling a transmission.

    config XYMODEM_CAN_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Maximum interval between consecutive <CAN> characters"
        range 1 1000
        default 100
        help
            Maximum interval, in milliseconds, allowed between two consecutive
            <CAN> characters when recognizing a cancellation request from the peer.

            X/YMODEM commonly uses two consecutive <CAN> characters to indicate
            transmission cancellation, but the protocol does not specify a maximum
            interval between them. A shorter interval reduces the chance of
            unrelated <CAN> characters being mistaken for a cancellation, while a
            longer interval improves compatibility with peers that transmit the
            characters with larger delays.

    config XYMODEM_PURGE_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "RX idle time required when purging received data (ms)"
        range 0 1000
        default 10
        help
            Specifies how long the receive path must remain idle before the
            RX purge operation is considered complete.

            While purging, all received data is discarded. The idle timer is
            effectively restarted whenever more data is received. Please Set
            this value based on the actual transmission rate of the underlying
            physical link.

endmenu